WEBVTT

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.000
Another job well done, sir!

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.220
<i>Thanks, it wasn't too bad today.</i>

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.840
I'm very glad we got the request.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.260
Or else we would've missed a meal!

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.470
You're right...

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.310
We only had a bottle
of ketchup in the fridge.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.940
<i>I'm sick of eating ketchup</i>
<i>and rice every day!</i>

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.530
<i>All right! Let's have</i>
<i>steak for dinner tonight!</i>

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.400
Sir, we can't just splurge like that.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.910
Our next request isn't confirmed yet.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Then, croquettes.</i>

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.410
That's reasonable.
It's cheap and delicious!

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:15.790
Sir?

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.920
Hey, stop that.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.260
Hey, quit that, will you?

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.390
Stop that! You're tickling me!

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.560
What are you doing?

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.810
Well...

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:16.540
MONSTER MANIA

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.540
I research the ecology
of life in this area.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:29.800
It's only a small portion
of the great Magmell,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:34.090
but it's filled with life, I discover
new creatures every day.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.430
I see.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:39.020
Despite its appearance,
this snake isn't poisonous

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.520
and is friendly with people.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.690
Cool.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.650
Go on, now. Thanks!

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.990
My name's Rubert.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.450
I'm Inyo.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:54.700
Nice to meet you.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.040
Check it out, Mr. Inyo!
It's a Steel Dragonfly!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.710
Their wings are hard like steel.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:04.960
Watch this!

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:10.920
See that?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:15.680
If you ever try to eat it, those wings
will cut you and give you a bloody mouth.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.510
And get this!

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.100
These wings have a Mohs' hardness of 10!

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.140
<i>It's the same hardness as diamonds!</i>

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:29.860
Fishman!

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.740
Got him! I got him!

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.200
Mr. Inyo, you're in luck.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.120
This is a rare one.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.660
See this? It's a fish with no gills.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.330
-<i>Sir, what's wrong with him?</i>
-They breathe through the lungs,

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.250
-He just loves life.
-just like humans!

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.800
That's the very reason why
they're able to live on land.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.510
These legs are evolved from their fins.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.050
Fascinating, isn't it?

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.510
Now, Mr. Inyo.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.680
Are you ready to go to my favorite place?

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.060
Don't hesitate, just follow me!

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.770
<i>There's no stopping him.</i>

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:10.020
Yup.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.030
Look! A Nibansenji!

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.570
And this one's the Snapping Bug!

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.660
<i>I don't think we should</i>
<i>get involved any further.</i>

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:17.950
Excuse Bird!

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.780
-Maybe so.
-Boring Cat!

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.420
Here we are.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.090
They're Encore Peckers' chicks.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.720
I'm looking after them since
their mother is missing.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:43.430
They've grown a lot.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.190
Here, it's lunch time.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:55.990
No need to rush.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.240
I've got one for everyone.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.460
-What was that?
-No!

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:10.960
Sir, that's--

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:11.880
<i>-Zero.</i>
-Yes, sir!

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.090
Don't breathe it in!

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:27.930
Are you okay?

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:30.020
How are the chicks?

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.030
They seem okay.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.780
Thank God.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.430
-Ready?
-Ready when you are!

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.350
Hey everyone! It's DJ Z and Baby FAT!

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:09.890
Yeah!

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:14.060
As you can see, we're back
in Magmell to do this again!

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.820
Our last episode was
a hit with 1,040,000 views.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.070
It's time for <i>Monster Darts!</i>

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.700
Couldn't you catch a bigger one?

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.450
Idiot, how are we supposed to do that?

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.240
This is too boring.

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:31.080
Just go with it. Hurry up and throw it!

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.580
All right. Make it look good.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.090
Here I go.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.840
Go!

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:45.850
Hallucinations?

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.260
Yup.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.640
If you breathe in the miasma it emits,
you'll see hallucinations.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.230
Really?

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.730
What was that you threw earlier?

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:59.110
A poppy seed.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.780
They love to eat them.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:05.780
But since I don't know much about it,

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.410
it disappears quickly after I Lacht it.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:14.290
I'm curious about
the composition of the miasma.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.460
-Ms. Zero, would you like some too?
-<i>Whoa! You scared me.</i>

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:21.970
Thanks for saving me earlier.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:24.380
<i>Oh, well, you know...</i>

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.800
It makes you hallucinate
the thing you dread the most.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.520
The thing you dread the most?

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:33.060
<i>If you breathe in the miasma,</i>

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:36.400
<i>you'll see your worst nightmare.</i>

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:38.860
Your worst nightmare?

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:44.150
Rubert?

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:48.370
Recently, there's been many
unfortunate events around here.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.040
Unfortunate?

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.870
The creatures around here in Magmell...

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:56.460
are dying in unnatural ways.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:57.750
<i>Unnatural ways?</i>

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.800
Yes, I've seen them nailed to a tree,

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:03.510
their mouths stuffed with stones...

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:05.550
and even chopped up into pieces.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:17.060
What do you think of the footage?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.190
Well, it could be better.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.230
It's gross and amazing!

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:23.650
Darts are a bit lame, don't you think?

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.860
What do you mean? You were so into it.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.820
Anything else we could do?

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:32.620
What's that?

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.000
It's a bird's nest.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.340
A bird's nest.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.800
-This is it!
-Wait, what?

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:47.720
-This is precisely what we're missing!
-What?

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:49.470
We're going to burn it!

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:50.640
What?

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:53.350
We're gonna burn it down
and make a spectacle out of it!

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.350
It'll be epic!

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.190
Are you serious?

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:58.390
Roll the camera!

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.360
DJ Z's <i>Three-Minute Cooking Show!</i>

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.740
Hey! Wait a minute.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.650
Today's dish is this!

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.620
Chargrilled Encore Pecker!

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.960
Now, let's get cooking, shall we?

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:22.380
Mr. Inyo! Ms. Zero! See you guys later!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.050
See you!

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.800
<i>Thank you for showing us around!</i>

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:29.630
It's burning!

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:31.590
The chicks!

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:39.060
-Burn! Burn!
-This is amazing...

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:40.980
Burn and disappear!

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.040
How could this be...

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.700
Why would this happen?

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:35.660
It's arson.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.160
It's too strong for a natural fire.
Someone intentionally started this fire.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:44.250
Who would do such a thing and why?

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:49.090
I can't answer that.
I didn't see anything either.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.840
You're right. I'm sorry, Mr. Inyo.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:00.930
-Zero.
<i>-Yes.</i>

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:17.950
Awesome! We burned it
to the ground! That's epic!

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.830
We somehow got away

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:24.120
but we were about to be burned alive too!

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.500
Who cares?

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:27.790
We got this epic footage!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.460
Yeah, but...

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:31.710
Shut up! It's done now, we're moving on.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:39.350
I'm sorry...

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.970
I couldn't protect you.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:48.820
-Now what?
-What?

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:52.740
-Don't you want to catch the perpetrator?
-What?

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.530
I found them, sir.

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:58.490
They stream videos as DJ Z and Baby FAT.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:00.370
They upload...

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.290
<i>What is this?</i>

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.040
<i>I'm sorry. It's just...</i>

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:09.130
<i>way worse than I expected.</i>

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:13.010
<i>Please hold on a minute.</i>

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.890
<i>I've located them! They're very close.</i>

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:20.680
Wait up!

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.060
Shut up and hurry up!

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:24.310
I'm the one carrying all the bags!

00:13:24.390 --> 00:13:25.730
Shut up already!

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:28.270
We found them.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:29.310
What?

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:30.900
They're in the vicinity.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:34.780
So what now?

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:43.910
Here it is.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:50.420
Let's get them.

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:02.100
-Stop right there!
-What?

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.680
Who the hell are you?

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.310
You guys burned the nest down, right?

00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:10.810
-They caught us.
-Idiot!

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:14.650
Why did you kill them?

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:16.400
Kill? Kill what?

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.110
The Encore Peckers!

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:19.700
Encore Peckers?

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:22.660
The birds you killed.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.870
Birds? Are there birds in Magmell?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.000
Only monsters live here, right?

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:35.090
Do you have any idea how hard
their parents work to raise their young?

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:40.090
Encore Peckers have many predators.
Only 10 percent of them

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:42.220
grow to become parents.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.010
So how could you...?

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:46.390
We're just one of those predators.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:52.400
That's right. We were one
of those predators too.

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:54.770
It is what it is, right?

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.900
-Don't you eat it?
-What?

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.320
Don't you eat grilled chicken?

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.120
Grilled chicken...?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.160
Don't you eat it all?
Pig, cow and chicken?

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:06.870
That's not the point.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.620
Yes! I like my grilled chicken
with barbeque sauce.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.460
That's why you're no good.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.540
It's all about the salt
when it comes to chicken.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:15.750
What? Just salt?

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:19.260
What are they even talking about?

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.800
Salt! Salt is the best!

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.010
What? But sauce is good too.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.810
Enough!

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:29.310
All these animals fight hard
to survive every day!

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.730
Even that Greasy Basilisk,

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:34.520
Mole Badger and the Steel Dragonfly,
they all have the right to live!

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:38.780
You guys have no right to
take away any lives!

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.450
-Don't you eat them?
-What?

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:44.700
I said, don't you eat chicken?

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:47.660
-That's not the point--
-You eat chicken, right?

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:53.290
So why do you get worked
up about that bird?

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.920
The only difference is
that we don't eat it.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.960
Don't you grill and eat chicken yourself?

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:04.640
I eat it.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.470
-Told you.
-I still think

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:11.270
barbeque sauce is the best.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.480
I love grilled chicken!

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:17.400
Mr. Rubert.

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:19.030
<i>Like I said...</i>

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:25.200
Burning and killing a bird or two
is nothing to fuss about.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:26.530
What?

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.450
Hey, how convenient.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:32.830
That one sweats out oil, right?

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.460
It'll burn well!

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.130
Let me show you.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.010
What are you waiting for?

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.100
Hurry and get the camera
before it burns all the way!

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.020
Hold on!

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:58.440
Apologize! Apologize to the chicks!

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.440
-Recognize your crime and redeem yourself!
-You bastard!

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.530
-Apologize!
-You idiot! What the hell are you doing?

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:05.490
-Come on! Apologize!
-Stop him!

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:13.700
Apologize.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.040
Mr. Rubert!

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.880
Are you going to stab me? Kill me?

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:21.210
No, you're just threatening me.
You have no intention to kill.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:22.340
Apologize!

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:24.970
I said, apologize!

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.970
Ta-da!

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:31.930
What?

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.020
The Greasy Basilisk is fine.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.890
It just got a little sunburned.

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:37.140
Mr. Inyo...?

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:40.570
Anyway, since you cooked it,
aren't you going to eat it?

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:41.570
What?

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:43.480
Go for it. It's seasoned with salt.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.990
Or is your mind set on
that barbeque sauce?

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:49.820
I'll shove it in your mouth.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.250
Hey! You idiot!

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:57.750
Don't leave me behind!

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:58.750
Apologize!

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:01.880
Why do I have to apologize?

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:04.260
You said you eat grilled chicken too!

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.470
There's no reason for you to
stoop down to their level.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.430
Mr. Inyo...

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.100
Anyway, we need to get out of here, quick.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:16.020
What?

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:18.270
Get out?

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.520
-A monster's on its way.
-What?

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:24.860
That guy ran towards the monster.
Hope he's all right.

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:31.450
You're full of it! I won't fall for that.

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:33.370
It's the truth.

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:39.250
-Shall we?
-Hey! What are you doing?

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:41.130
-But the monster...
-Hurry up and let me loose!

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.630
-Don't worry.
-The monster's coming!

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:45.210
He's only facing his worst nightmare.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.880
Let me loose!

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:50.130
What do you mean, my worst nightmare?

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:54.720
Go away!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:57.480
Get away... Get away from me!

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:03.810
-See you later!
-What?

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.940
It's not gonna rain,
so you'll be all right.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.360
Hey that's not the issue here!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:10.780
Untie me now!

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:13.490
Hey! You can't leave me here!

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:17.160
Who do they think they are? Unbelievable.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.380
What. What's that?

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:34.640
What? This is the monster?

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.060
See? I knew he was lying.

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:41.520
Don't underestimate me!

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.650
Stop it! Ouch!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.900
-Sorry--
-I wonder what he's hallucinating about.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.450
Everyone has their own fears.

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:12.590
<i>Stop!</i>

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:16.600
<i>I uploaded it on their channel.</i>

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:18.430
<i>It's getting a lot of views.</i>

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.850
Thank you for everything.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:24.440
I doubt they'll come back again.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:26.270
Mr. Inyo.

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:30.990
I must admit.
I was ready to kill those guys.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:35.360
I'm such a hypocrite,
preaching to them not to steal lives.

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.120
It's fine.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:39.450
-What?
-Don't feel guilty about your thoughts.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.290
You didn't actually kill them.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:55.220
Goodbye, Mr. Inyo! Goodbye, Ms. Zero!

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.720
<i>Sir!</i>

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:04.980
<i>Sir, do you not enjoy being an Angler?</i>

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:09.400
Zero, do you really think I could
make a living doing something else?

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:16.910
<i>Zero? You said we only have</i>
<i>ketchup in the house, right?</i>

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.910
<i>This is... Well...</i>

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:23.370
I want steak for dinner tonight.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:26.460
<i>Steak? That's... well...</i>

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:29.080
I'm kidding. I'm good with croquettes.

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:30.590
<i>Sir!</i>

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:34.840
Let's go shopping as soon as I get back.

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:36.380
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:13.020
PREVIEW

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.240
<i>It's unbelievable!</i>
<i>Master actually woke up early!</i>

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:21.070
<i>He never wakes up</i>
<i>no matter how many alarms I set</i>

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:23.240
<i>and no matter how many lemons</i>
<i>I squeeze onto his face!</i>

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:25.410
<i>But today, he woke up on his own!</i>

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:27.160
<i>How suspicious...</i>

00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:30.040
<i>What is he up to?</i>

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:32.000
<i>I'm dying...</i>

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.210
<i>I'm dying to know!</i>

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:39.130
<i>Next time, "Bonded ZERO." Don't miss it.</i>

00:23:39.550 --> 00:23:41.550
Subtitle translation by Sachiko Takahashi
